Good point about rate limiting. We could reduce the maximum retries or even implement a notification if the retries exceed a certain threshold. As for the nested objects, by flattening them into separate rows, our schema in BigQuery will have additional tables or columns dedicated to these details, like subscription items. This approach keeps the data atomic and easier to query for specific insights.

